  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Working Reader",
    "overview": "The app is the student's own marked-up copy of the paper. A bright white sheet of bond paper lies on a cool grey desk; the shell around it is a binder-cobalt rail. Ink is black, marginalia and cancels are pencil grey, and colour enters only as highlighter: the voice sweeps the sentence it reads in yellow, and every capture sticks out of the page edge as a small coloured flag at its sentence, mirrored along the top of the timeline.\n\nDensity is that of a working document, not a showcase. Hairline rules divide everything; surfaces are paper panels with 4px corners and no lift. The reading column is the product and is defended at every width: tools appear beside it and recede. The interface speaks in Atkinson Hyperlegible, the paper speaks in Literata, and every number is set in tabular figures.\n\nThe world refuses the category default for reading tools: a grey sidebar, a blue selection highlight, and a notes panel of rounded cards.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White paper sheet on a cool grey desk, cobalt rail as the shell.",
      "Highlighter fluorescents carry meaning, never decoration.",
      "Captures are flags and ruled marginalia, not cards.",
      "Changes cancel in pencil and can be undone; nothing silently disappears.",
      "Two bundled faces: Atkinson Hyperlegible for interface, Literata for reading.",
      "Hairline rules and 4px corners; one soft shadow, reserved for the sheet and popovers."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Highlighter Rule",
        "body": "Fluorescents appear only for reading (the yellow sweep) and the four capture types (note green, quote blue, card pink, mark orange). Never on status chips, buttons, navigation or decoration. Never two highlighter fills in one region of text: a sentence carries one highlight at a time. Flags, flag strips, timeline ticks and the four capture keys are the capture index and show each type in its own colour as a small tab.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Cobalt Rule",
        "body": "Cobalt is the shell. It is not an accent for buttons or links on paper; primary actions are ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Form-Not-Colour Rule",
        "body": "State is carried by an icon and a word as well as colour: every chip has its icon, every cancel its strike-through.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Literata is for the paper and anything quoted from it (sheet, printed/read columns, captured quotes, card faces). Atkinson is for everything the app says. Never mix them within one line of interface.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every number (counts, times, pages, sizes, percentages) is set with tabular lining figures (`tnum`, `lnum`).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Column Wins Rule",
        "body": "The reading column never collapses. Panels collapse first, then labels, then the rail narrows.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Sheet Rule",
        "body": "A soft offset shadow belongs only to the paper sheet and to popovers. Panels, steps, rows and cards are flat with a hairline. No hard offset shadows anywhere.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep the reading column at full measure (66ch) and collapse the panel, labels and rail before it.",
      "**Do** use exactly one highlighter per meaning: yellow for being read; green note, blue quote, pink card, orange mark.",
      "**Do** draw captures as ruled marginalia with a hanging flag.",
      "**Do** cancel instead of deleting: pencil strike-through plus undo for switched-off changes and removed captures.",
      "**Do** set every number in tabular figures.",
      "**Do** carry state with icon and word: ready is an outline with a check, in progress an ink-outline pill, warning an outline in Wait Umber, error an error wash.",
      "**Do** use Literata for anything from the paper and Atkinson Hyperlegible for everything the app says."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put highlighter fluorescents on status chips, buttons or decoration, or two highlighter fills in one region.",
      "**Don't** box captures as cards or nest a card inside a card.",
      "**Don't** make a status chip look like a filled button.",
      "**Don't** give a shadow to anything but the paper sheet and popovers; never a hard offset shadow.",
      "**Don't** use cobalt as an accent on paper; primary actions are ink.",
      "**Don't** silently remove anything the user or the rules changed.",
      "**Don't** use uppercase tracked labels or kickers above headings."
